/*
 * Declares the DefContext class, which tracks semantic-validation state
 * specific to `def` declarations. This context is used to detect recursive
 * dependencies between definitions and to ensure that `def` symbols are
 * validated in a safe and dependency-aware order.
 *
 * The DefContext maintains a recursion-level table for all `def` symbols
 * currently being validated. This prevents infinite recursion when `def`
 * declarations reference each other cyclically and allows the validator to
 * determine when a definition may be safely validated or must be deferred.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::validator::context::def_
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/validator/context/def_.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-03-18
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
